           "source_section": "Statement",
           "quote": "Assume AC and the feature-measure energy hypotheses. Let $r_0>0$ and let $\\mu_0\\in\\mathcal P_2(\\Omega)$ have finite energy and be concentrated on $Q_{r_0}$. Set $M_0=\\sup\\{\\|\\nabla R(z)\\|:R(z)\\le F(\\mu_0)\\}$, $a=(1+M_0)C_1$, and $b=(1+M_0)C_2$. For $T<\\infty$, define\n$$r(T)=\\begin{cases}(r_0+aT),&b=0,\\\\(r_0+a/b)e^{bT}-a/b,&b>0.\\end{cases}$$\nFor every $R>r(T)$, the localized flow with indicator $\\iota_{Q_R}$ remains in $Q_{r(T)}$ for $0\\le t\\le T$ and therefore solves the continuity equation with the constraint $\\Omega$ alone on this interval. Localized flows with different cutoffs larger than $r(T)$ agree on $[0,T]$. In particular no trajectory starting in $Q_{r_0}$ can escape every cutoff in finite time.",
